# Retire policy 2026-11-20: still in production in 2026 with no announced end; retire dates commented out. Revisit when an end is announced.
# Renault Megane E-Tech Electric five-door crossover, 2022 onwards.
#
# The "Megane V" as sold in Britain. From 2022 the only Megane on sale here was
# the Megane E-Tech Electric: the combustion Megane IV was withdrawn in July
# 2022 and the French-market petrol Megane V hatchback was never offered in
# Britain. It is a crossover-styled car, 1.505 m tall against 1.447 m for the
# Megane IV hatch and 160 mm shorter overall, and that British car is what is
# modelled, not the French hatchback.
# https://www.autocar.co.uk/ (18 July 2022, cited in the reference pack)
#
# Dimensions 4.199 x 1.768 x 1.505 m, wheelbase 2.685 m. Source: the reference
# pack's notes. The hull measures 4.199 x 1.768 m on a 2.685 m wheelbase (63.9
# per cent); mirrors take the width to 1.910 m.
#
# Shape reference: no true side elevation of this car exists on Commons. The
# flank was built from the widest available view (about 35-40 degrees forward
# of the side axis) plus front and rear three-quarters, with the wheel centres
# fixed by the published ratio; a true elevation was rendered and has no
# photograph to match. All glazing panes stand 10-18 mm clear of the local body
# surface.
#
# Colours are from the Renault UK Megane E-Tech brochure of December 2022,
# evidence grade (a): Glacier White (non-metallic); Diamond Black, Shadow Grey,
# Ceramic Grey, Flame Red and Midnight Blue (metallic). Two-tone roofs in
# Diamond Black or Shadow Grey were offered from Techno trim; the model keeps a
# single body colour. Renault UK renamed the global press-kit colours (Rafale
# Grey, Schist Grey) as Ceramic Grey and Shadow Grey for this market, and the
# British names are the ones recorded. Four are modelled: Glacier White,
# Diamond Black, Shadow Grey and Flame Red. Weights white 3, black 2, grey 3,
# red 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# The gold "F1 blade" in the front bumper carries its own material and is not
# affected by the body recolouring.
#
# Speed 160 km/h, the car's governed maximum. Comfort 115/503, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 115: quiet, smooth and roomy for its size. Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: July 2022 intro, retire dates commented out (still in production in 2026)
# fourteen- to seventeen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/renault-megane-v.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/renault-megane-v.dae (105 objects). References:
# citycars/references/renault-megane-v/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the nose is squarer and the lamp surrounds more angular
# than the photographs, and the camera matches are approximate because no side
# elevation exists. At 128 px the raised crossover stance, the full-width light
# bars and the flush surfaces read as the Megane E-Tech.

obj=citycar
name=RenaultMeganeV(GlacierWhite)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=2022
intro_month=7
#retire_year=2039
#retire_month=6
speed=160
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=115
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=503

Image[E]=./images/renault-megane-v-glacierwhite_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/renault-megane-v-glacierwhite_SE.0.0,-13,0
